# CIVITA public distribution repo.
#
# This file works by EXPLICIT DENY, not by an allowlist. The private working repo
# uses `*` + `!allowed` — which excludes the configured build only by not listing
# it. That is a silent guard: loosen the allowlist once and a live Supabase key
# ships. Here, the deny rules below hold no matter what else is added.

# --- HARD: never publish a build with the backend config filled in ---------
# The distributed CIVITA-v9.html must ship with CENTRAL_DB_URL and
# CENTRAL_DB_ANON_KEY blank. The manager fills them only in a private copy.
*-configured.html
*configured*.html
SUPABASE*.txt
*.env
.env*

# --- Local noise -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
